  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this problem. The archive has other PowerShell 7 startup crashes that exit with 0x80131623. Those fail in InitialSessionState (terminal#16660, #16301, #17467) or in PSReadLine, so they are different problems. Your stack trace shows the crash is in pwsh itself, not in Windows Terminal. The update-notification banner in `UpdatesNotification.ShowUpdateNotification` calls `PadRight` with a negative width (-17). That probably happens because the console is very narrow when the window first opens, so the width calculation goes negative. Try these steps:\\n1. Disable the update check by setting the environment variable `POWERSHELL_UPDATECHECK=Off`. You can also launch with `pwsh -NoProfile` to confirm.\\n2. Update PowerShell to a newer build.\\n3. Report the bug to the PowerShell repository (github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell). Include your Terminal profile, font and window size, and say that it happens when a new window opens.\\n4. If it keeps happening, file a new Terminal ticket with the profile settings.\"}",
